  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0070 database is a comprehensive system for managing user accounts, content, and interactions within a community or platform. At its core, it contains a users table, which stores information about each registered user, including their login credentials, personal details, and preferences. Each user can have multiple social sign-on (SSO) accounts linked to their main account, as recorded in the user_ssos table. Users can participate in discussions and create content, which is stored in the topics table, where each topic is associated with a specific user, node, and section. Users can also create replies to existing topics, which are stored in the replies table, and these replies can be linked to specific users and topics. The team_users table links users to teams, while the team_id column in the topics table indicates which team is associated with each topic. The pages table stores information about static pages, including their title, body, and version history, which is tracked in the page_versions table. The oauth_applications table manages third-party applications that can interact with the platform, and the oauth_access_tokens and oauth_access_grants tables handle authentication and authorization for these applications. The notifications table keeps track of notifications sent to users, and the notes table stores personal notes created by users. The nodes table represents a hierarchical structure of content, with each node linked to a specific section. The locations table stores information about geographic locations, and the exception_tracks table logs any exceptions or errors that occur within the system. Finally, the devices table tracks user devices and their associated tokens, and the comments table stores comments made by users on various content items, while the authorizations table manages user authorizations with external providers.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves the development of \"Homeland,\" an open-source discussion platform built using Ruby on Rails. The platform serves as a full-stack forum application and is designed to provide users with an efficient and user-friendly discussion experience. It integrates social networking features, real-time notifications, and supports responsive design to accommodate various devices.\n\n Objectives\n\nThe primary goal of Homeland is to offer a robust platform for online discussions. It aims to facilitate user interaction through features like topic following, notifications, and content mention. Additionally, it seeks to enable secure deployment and integration with other systems via Single Sign-On (SSO) and public APIs.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Administrators: Manage content, users, and system settings.\n- End Users: Participate in discussions, follow topics, and engage with content.\n- Developers: Use the public API for building applications.\n- System Integrators: Implement SSO for seamless integration with other systems.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Forum Capabilities:\n   - Users can create, reply to, and follow topics.\n   - Real-time notifications keep users updated on activity.\n   - Topics and posts can be formatted using Markdown.\n   - Users can mention others using a syntax similar to Twitter.\n\n2. Responsive Design:\n   - The platform is accessible on desktops, tablets, and mobile devices.\n   - Layout adjusts automatically to different screen sizes.\n\n3. Social Networking Integration:\n   - Users can follow other users and specific topics.\n   - Supports Twemoji and system emojis for engagement.\n\n4. Security and SSO:\n   - Automated free SSL integration for secure access via HTTPS.\n   - Supports SSO as both provider and consumer for account synchronization across systems.\n\n5. Public API:\n   - Provides an API for developing mobile applications and integrating with other services.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Quick response times for page loading and user interactions.\n- Scalability: Efficiently handle a large number of users and discussions.\n- Security: Data encryption and secure authentication mechanisms.\n- Usability: Intuitive user interface with an emphasis on ease of use for all functionalities.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0070.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0070\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_hash` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_ssos` (\n  `sso_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `provider` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `provider_user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sso_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ssos_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `topics` (\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `node_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`topic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `topics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `topics_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`node_id`) REFERENCES `nodes` (`node_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `topics_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `replies` (\n  `reply_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reply_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `replies_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `replies_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`topic_id`) REFERENCES `topics` (`topic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team_users` (\n  `team_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `team_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`team_user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `team_users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `team_users_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`team_id`) REFERENCES `teams` (`team_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pages` (\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`page_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `page_versions` (\n  `version_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `page_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `version` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`version_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `page_versions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`page_id`) REFERENCES `pages` (`page_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `oauth_applications` (\n  `app_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `client_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `client_secret` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`app_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `oauth_access_tokens` (\n  `token_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `expires_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`token_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `oauth_access_tokens_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`app_id`) REFERENCES `oauth_applications` (`app_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `oauth_access_tokens_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `oauth_access_grants` (\n  `grant_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `app_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `grant` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`grant_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `oauth_access_grants_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`app_id`) REFERENCES `oauth_applications` (`app_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `oauth_access_grants_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notes` (\n  `note_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`note_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `nodes` (\n  `node_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `section_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `parent_node_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`node_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `nodes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`section_id`) REFERENCES `sections` (`section_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `locations` (\n  `location_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,8) NOT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(11,8) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`location_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `exception_tracks` (\n  `exception_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `message` text NOT NULL,\n  `stack_trace` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exception_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `devices` (\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `device_token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`device_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `devices_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `topic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`topic_id`) REFERENCES `topics` (`topic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `authorizations` (\n  `authorization_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `provider` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `provider_user_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`authorization_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `authorizations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
